What:           /sys/devices/platform/1500b000.video-codec/state
Date:           October 2026
Contact:        FuQuan233
Description:
                Read-only codec buffer bridge counters: successful coherent
                allocations and DMA-BUF imports, cumulative VMA mappings
                (including fork/split), and currently live VMAs, buffers and
                page-rounded charged bytes. A released handle with an active
                coherent mapping still counts as live until its last unmap.
                Counters are individually sampled. Reading does not access
                MMIO, enable VCODEC clocks, or submit a codec DMA operation.

                The second line reports active-job state and cumulative jobs,
                real IRQ completions, WAIT timeouts, explicit cancellations,
                spurious interrupts and runtime-PM failures. The third reports
                a latched device fault, real ISP-domain OFF generations and
                failures to establish a fresh OFF after an aborted job. A fault
                retains the possible DMA objects and wake source until reboot;
                these counters are observations, never simulated completion.
